{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/833813-trouble-with-the-lancea-et-sanctum","id":833813,"title":"Trouble with the Lancea et Sanctum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-20T06:59:50-08:00","id":833813,"title":"Trouble with the Lancea et Sanctum","content":"So, I'm having som difficulty in understanding the details of the Lancea et Sanctum. Or more to the point; I can't seem to find them.<br /> I get that they are the church, that they seek out sinners and I get their holy cause.<br /> Now they follow the teachings of Longinus, yes? But I can't seem to find the teachings they follow? Are there commandments or codes of conduct specific to the Sanctified? <br /> I want my players to have the details, so they have the chance to interpret the writings themselves instead of ONLY having the ST tell them what the doctrines mean.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I will tell them how they've been schooled - but whatever else the Sanctified may be, they do have their own inner thoughts and workings <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So my question is: Can anyone here help me with the teachings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3448-monkeymann","name":"MonkeyMann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T07:21:28-08:00","id":833820,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/62830\" target=\"_blank\">The Testament of Longinus</a> might be a good place to start. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In a nutshell, Longinian doctrine teaches that vampires are damned by God, but they still have a place in His plan. They have been chosen to act as the predators that meanace His flock, strengthening their faith in the process. The Sanctified therefore protect the faithful and punish the sinners. Some also see it as their duty to act as persecutor, as was Satan's role - to tempt the faithful into sedition and punish those who fall to temptation. Others see this interpretation as heretical.<br /> <br /> Another big thing that has become part of the Lancea et Sanctum's identity in Second Edition is their role ad lore keepers. With the fog of eternity being less of a sure thing now, the Sanctified have to work harder to make sure their version of history is the version people believe, so they seek out ancient historical and holy texts, so that they can put the ones that support their views into the holy archives and dispose of the ones that undermine their views. That's not really a Longinian thing though, so much as a thing modern Sanctified do to make Longinus' dogma look stronger.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The Lancea et Sanctum Covenant Book is also a good resource. It's 1st edition, but the fiction is pretty much all still relevant and the mechanics could be converted if you wanted to use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-20-2016, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T07:40:41-08:00","id":833826,"title":"","content":"As with most religions, the L+S does interpret things differently and since there is no central authority (like a vampire Pope or College of Cardinals) interpretations can differ from domain to domain, bishop to bishop, priest to priest, layperson to layperson.<br /> <br /> As Charlaquin said, generally their divinely ordained duties can be separated into: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Scourge humanity. Give humanity a taste of Hell, so that Heaven may appear even sweeter in comparison.</li> <li>Tempt humanity. Only the truly Faithful may see the Glory of the Kingdom of God.</li> <li>Protect the faithful. Visit retribution on those who would harm those that enjoy His grace.</li> </ol><br /> Those are the roles that vampires are meant to fulfill in God's plan. Both wolves and shepherds to humanity. Everything about the vampiric condition stems from these. Vampires are powerful and coercive to do these things, yet they are also scourged by Banes so that they may not rise up and place themselves as Masters of Man instead of their predators. Of course, even His ordained predators may sometimes err and that is where the Sanctified's spiritual guidance and counselling comes in.<br /> <br /> Which of these three duties is most important and what to do when two or more are in conflict? That is up to individual dogma.<br /> <br /> A small warning, the Testament that Charlaquin linked is technically 1e, so the portrayal of some parts of the vampiric condition might not fully align with 2e any more, but the differences should be fairly small and hard to notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T07:50:02-08:00","id":833829,"title":"","content":"Pretty much what Charlaquin said. There's the holy book in pdf form for you. <br /> <br /> Another thing to reverse engineer doctrine based on abilities. The Lancea Sanctum get super library merits, inspiring lectures, and certain rituals that follow a theme in the core book. <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles-playtest-vampire-the-requiem/\" target=\"_blank\">This link has more stuff</a>, including witch hunters, sanctuaries for outlaws, Stigmata bleeding that inspires, Temples that give bonuses to Theban sorcery, and some rather interesting new rituals that encourage deviance. &quot;What do these things tell us about what the LeS believe?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}